 ## Background
-3D Gaussian Splatting was introduced by Kerbl et al. in 2023 [9]. It builds on the concept of radiance fields but uses explicit 3D Gaussians instead of implicit neural networks. The method was inspired by the need for real-time rendering of complex 3D scenes. The original 3DGS initializes positions using sparse point clouds from SfM tools like COLMAP [21] [S2]. It has since become a popular alternative to NeRF for 3D reconstruction and novel view synthesis.
